-- Q5805: Data Protection Technologies [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Per NIST SP 800-113, SFTP operates over SSH using a single encrypted channel on port 22, simplifying firewall rules. FTPS wraps TLS around the traditional FTP protocol, which uses separate control and data channels requiring more complex firewall configurations with dynamic port ranges.
Wrong (A): Both SFTP and FTPS provide data encryption. SFTP uses SSH encryption while FTPS uses TLS encryption; neither transmits data in cleartext.
Wrong (B): File size support is not inherently different between the protocols. SSH compression is optional and does not expand maximum file size limits.
Wrong (C): SFTP is not inherently slower than FTPS. SSH compression is optional, and both protocols have comparable throughput for bulk file transfers.$EXPL$
