-- Q5806: Data Protection Technologies [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per NIST SP 800-88 Rev. 1 and HIPAA 45 CFR 164.530(j), organizations must follow documented retention schedules and securely destroy records after the retention period expires. Destruction certificates provide verifiable evidence of proper sanitization for regulatory compliance.
Wrong (B): Retaining data indefinitely because it is encrypted does not satisfy retention schedule obligations. Encryption does not exempt an organization from destroying data that has exceeded its mandated retention period.
Wrong (C): Moving records to cheaper storage still constitutes retention beyond the mandated period, increasing breach liability and regulatory exposure.
Wrong (D): Removing encryption keys (cryptographic erasure) alone is insufficient. Formal sanitization with documented destruction evidence is required for HIPAA compliance.$EXPL$
