-- Q5807: Data Protection Technologies [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Per NIST SP 800-101 Rev. 1, steganography is the practice of concealing data within other non-secret media files such as images, audio, or video, making the hidden information invisible to casual observers. Unlike encryption, which makes data unreadable, steganography hides the very existence of the data.
Wrong (A): Data masking replaces sensitive values with fictitious but realistic substitutes. It does not embed hidden data within carrier files like images.
Wrong (C): Tokenization replaces sensitive data with non-sensitive tokens mapped through a secure vault. It does not involve hiding data within media files.
Wrong (D): Code obfuscation makes source code harder to understand but does not hide data within carrier files. It transforms code representation rather than embedding secret content.$EXPL$
